      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just as a note-- \"stilts\" results from the avatar's legs being too long in comparison to the other proportions on the avatar, not from your own height. Your IRL height doesn't have too much to do with how an avatar calibrates.\n\nI'd strongly suggest taking a look at our docs, where we list the Rigging Requirements for Full-Body Tracking compatibility. \n\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/docs/full-body-tracking#section-rigging-requirements",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-09-29T01:22:15.795Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Full body tracking is getting better everyday yes? So why is it so difficult to get the proportions to fix itself. Many people use the playspace mover to buy the feet on the ground and height change to get to the head. But what if like,instead, the trackers are automatically set to where the ankles,head,and hips are placed. I'm 4'11 and there arent avatars my size that often and it would be great to have some kind of toggle to not care about your own body proportion instead of feeling like I'm on stilts all the time.",
